    ],
    "text": "Remarkably, despite the different motivations behind our models, all three produce nearly equal values for the maximal seasonal throughput of the river, with between 1150 and 1250 customers served each season when there are 100 campsites along the river. In the best of all situations, the itinerary model can reach up to 1400 customers per season with nearly 100% campsite utilization, though this does introduce a great deal of crowding. Thus, we can con- \ufb01dently say that no matter the approach the river managers choose to take, they can expect a maximum throughput in this range."
  },
